        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If there was a simple solution they could implement I'm sure it would already be in. &nbsp; They are aware of it and have commented on other posts about this.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Multiple times in fact, for me this, though would be neat, is not mandatory. It's been talked often enough I'm surprised there isn't an answer in the FAQ :P. &nbsp;Hopefully a way to toggle the FF button on and off, so you don't always have to move your finger for mobile and tablet, slowing down the game.</p>\n<p>It's just a thought.&nbsp;</p>",
